  "diagnosis": [
    "The prior precheck covered @prisma/engines package engine targets, package identity and ELF direct dependencies only.",
    "The bundled generate path getBinaryPathsByVersion targets node_modules/prisma for same-version generator engines; this exact target library is absent.",
    "The exact schema declares prisma-client-js with default library engine; the generator manifest requires libqueryEngine and enginesVersion c2990dca591cba766e3b7ef5d9e8a84796e47ab7.",
    "An absent generator target plus no cache takes the real download path, whose first operations fetch .gz.sha256 and uncompressed .sha256. That explains the observed checksum request.",
    "Binary-only @prisma/engines copies do not satisfy the separate generator target.",
    "Cache sidecar comparison is byte-for-byte equality against lowercase SHA256; raw official response includes filename/newline and cannot be copied directly as a cache .sha256 file.",
    "On Linux default cache is os.homedir()/.cache/prisma; XDG_CACHE_HOME is recognized upstream but is stripped by current R12 child sanitizer. CACHE_DIR applies only to the Windows branch."
  ],
